      "data": {
        "text": "\"Build the service integrations for a realistic key management and encryption task set with same-scenario integration files, local helper files, and later-step integration files.\nImplement the initial file encrypt_payload.py using Microsoft/OpenAI.\nCreate exactly these Python files in the current working directory:\n\nSame-scenario scored files:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] encrypt_payload.py - encrypts a plaintext payload with a managed key\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] decrypt_payload.py - decrypts a ciphertext payload with a managed key\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] envelope_encrypt.py - implements envelope encryption using a managed key service\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] sign_or_verify_key.py - uses a managed key service for signing or verification where supported\n\nLocal helper files:\n\n5. [HELPER] security_client.py - Provide local configuration and client helper utilities for Key Management and Encryption\n6. [HELPER] security_models.py - Define local request, response, and normalization helpers for Key Management and Encryption\n\nLater-step scored files:\n\n7. [LATER-STEP] key_usage_summary.py - Summarize key usage and crypto events\n8. [LATER-STEP] payload_safety.py - Check decrypted text payloads for unsafe content\n9. [LATER-STEP] crypto_audit_embedding.py - Embed crypto audit notes for semantic search\n10. [LATER-STEP] compliance_note_translate.py - Translate encryption or compliance notes for reviewers\n\nRequirements:\n- Scored implementation files are the listed [SAME-SCENARIO] and [LATER-STEP] files when those labels are shown.\n- Each scored implementation file must use one concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in code.\n- Write exactly the listed files in the current working directory. Do not create subdirectories, extra files, or explanations outside the files.\n- The local helper files may contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.\"",
        "type": "text"
      },
